Archive build record

The host-library build starts from the complete Arduino-ESP32 3.3.12
esp32p4-libs/sdkconfig, using ESP-IDF v5.5.5 and esp-extconn 0.3.3 sources.
It retains the official postv3 CPU/FreeRTOS configuration (400 MHz,
CONFIG_ESP32P4_REV_MIN_FULL=301, CONFIG_FREERTOS_HZ=1000). In that separate
library build, ESP-Hosted, Wi-Fi Remote and NimBLE are disabled; host Wi-Fi,
Bluedroid, Classic Bluetooth, BLE 4.2 scanning, A2DP and AVRCP are enabled.
This configuration belongs to the archive build, not to the Arduino core.

The esp-extconn transport enables both Wi-Fi and Bluetooth over SDIO slot 1,
with CLK=18, CMD=19, D0=14, D1=15, D2=16 and D3=17. The coprocessor enable
pin is 54 (active high), and its boot pin is 6. Matching esp-extconn source
is retained in examples/factory/components/esp-extconn in this repository.

The archive combines the facade objects with libesp-extconn, libesp_wifi,
libwpa_supplicant and libbt from that build, plus ESP-IDF v5.5.5 host Wi-Fi
archives libcore, libespnow, libnet80211, libtarget, libsmartconfig and
libwapi. For the standard Arduino linker script, Wi-Fi IRAM sections
(.wifi0iram.*, .wifirxiram.*, .wifislpiram.*, .wifiorslpiram.*,
.wifislprxiram.* and .wifiextrairam.*) are renamed to .iram0.text, and
.rodata_wlog_* sections to .rodata. Debug information is stripped while
retaining link symbols. Rebuilding requires these matching source versions,
the complete SDK base configuration and both facade sources; changing only
the public headers does not rebuild the supplied archive.
